# Build context exclusions. Every image in this repo builds with `context: .`
# (services/*/Dockerfile and the legacy root Dockerfile), so without this file
# the whole working tree — host caches, virtualenvs, screenshots and the real
# .env — is uploaded to the daemon and anything a COPY happens to cover is
# baked into the published image.
#
# Two jobs:
#
#   1. Keep the real .env out of the context. No Dockerfile copies it today and
#      this file is what keeps that true. It matters more than it looks: every
#      service's config.py calls _load_dotenv(".env") against its WORKDIR at
#      import time, so a .env that ever reached /app would silently become live
#      configuration — including whatever credentials the developer had in it.
#
#   2. Keep host build junk and tests out of the images. The Dockerfiles COPY
#      whole directories (packages/sdk-py/, services/<svc>/), which on a local
#      build drags in the developer's __pycache__ (compiled against a different
#      interpreter and shadowing the copied sources on import), *.egg-info, and
#      every service's tests/ — dead weight in a published image.
#
# Nothing here excludes a config default: detectors.yml, voice-pricing.yml and
# docs/config/*.yml are now COPY'd into the images that read them, so each image
# boots correctly configured and the compose bind mounts of those same paths are
# genuine overrides rather than the only source of the file. Excluding any of
# them from this context would silently take that default back out.

# VCS and CI metadata — never copied, and .git is the largest thing in the tree.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Python bytecode, build output and tool caches
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# Virtualenvs. A host .venv is built for the host's OS/arch and is at best dead
# weight, at worst a broken import path shadowing the image's own site-packages.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Secrets. .env.example is only documentation, but nothing copies it either.
.env
.env.*

# Tests. No runtime import path reaches them and they only inflate the image —
# ~7.8MB off the api image alone (services/api/tests + packages/sdk-py/tests +
# packages/schemas-py/tests). services/explainer is the one exception: that
# image exists solely to run its own suite (its CMD is
# `pytest services/explainer/tests/`), so excluding them would break it.
# A .dockerignore is per-CONTEXT, not per-Dockerfile, so this exception also
# leaves explainer's 344KB of tests in the three images that COPY
# services/explainer/ (alerts, api, semantic). That is the cheaper half of the
# trade against breaking the one Dockerfile whose whole purpose is those tests.
**/tests/
!services/explainer/tests/

# Node
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
*.tgz

# Local artefacts that are in the tree but in no image: screenshots, the
# vendored deepeval wheel (services/semantic installs it from PyPI, not here),
# the audit working directory and the extracted/ scratch tree.
*.png
*.whl
audit/
extracted/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
